WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.130
Each member of the Madrigal family from Disney's
"Encanto" is given a gift that reflects their

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:07.890
personality and can be used to help the community.

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:11.380
Yet not all of the Madrigals' gifts are equally
useful.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:16.930
Many adults will notice this seems to be especially
true of Mirabel's, who has been given the

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:19.320
miraculous power to control the weather.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:23.881
While this would normally be an incredible
gift, Pepa isn't like Storm from "X-Men" who

00:00:23.881 --> 00:00:26.179
can summon rain and wind at will.

00:00:26.179 --> 00:00:30.989
Instead, she's a bundle of emotions whose
mood is reflected in the weather she conjures.

00:00:30.989 --> 00:00:36.300
As a result, throughout "Encanto," Pepa is
seen with clouds hovering above her head signifying

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:39.880
the anxiety she seems to feel almost constantly.

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:44.100
Pepa's gift is well suited to her stressed
out personality, given how deep her emotions

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.100
seem to run.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:49.539
However, it appears Pepa hasn't managed to
harness her feelings in a way that enables

00:00:49.539 --> 00:00:52.710
her to turn her gift to anyone's advantage.

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:54.649
She's honestly kind of a wreck.

00:00:54.649 --> 00:00:59.372
And that's something most kid viewers probably
didn't notice — but the adults watching sure did.

